{title: 276 - Thanks to God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #276 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 276}
{meta: category Holy Scriptures - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Thanks to God whose [F]Word [Gm]was [Am]spoken
[C7]In [Am]the [C7/Bb]deed that made [Dm]the earth.
[Am]His the voice [Gm]that [Bb]called [Gm/D]a [A7/Db]nation;
[Edim]His the [Dm]fires [Gm]that [Edim]tried her [C]worth.
[F]God has [Am]spoken;
[Gm]Praise Him for [F/C]His open Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Thanks to God whose [F]Word [Gm]incarnate
[C7]Glorified the flesh [F/C]of [Dm]man.
[Am]Deeds and words [Gm]and [Bb]death [Gm/D]and [A7/Db]rising
[Edim]Tell the [Dm]grace [Gm]in heaven's [C]plan.
[F]God has [Am]spoken;
[Gm]Praise Him for [F/C]His open Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Thanks to God whose [F]Word [Gm]is [Am]answered
[C7]By [Am]the [C7/Bb]Spirit's voice [Dm]wihin.
[Am]Here we drink [Gm]of [Bb]joy [Gm/D]unmeasured,
[Edim]Life redeemed [Gm]from death [Edim]and [C]sin.
[F]God is [Am]speaking;
[Gm]Praise Him for [F/C]His open Word.
{end_of_verse}
